     "insertText": {
      "text": " Metagenomic abundance is the percentage of the reads of eight single-copy ribosomal-protein genes whose best DIAMOND hit is a reference genome of the genus (GTDB R232); Halomonas includes Vreelandella, which GTDB separates from it, and Clostridium includes the GTDB genera with Clostridium suffixes (e.g. Clostridium_B). Only 8% of the reads assigned to Clostridium had a best hit at least 95% identical, so that assignment is uncertain. MAG abundance is the percentage of all reads that mapped to the genus’s species in the re-assembled MAG set; no species of Idiomarina, Clostridium or Marinilabilia was recovered. In the metagenomic and MAG rows, letters show Dunn’s tests (Holm-adjusted) after a significant Kruskal–Wallis test across the four sites (p < 0.05); sites sharing a letter do not differ.",
      "location": {
       "index": 120979
      }
     }
